# mix-of-capabilities §8.1 P1 — 08×09 accesso relazionale × deduzione (e 06 per le
# proprieta' insegnate parlando). La domanda chiede una proprieta' che nessun
# fatto dice del soggetto: la risposta viene dalla sua classe (is_a, has_prop) e
# ne dice il perche'. Il «No» solo con la proprieta' opposta tenuta dalla classe.
[mock live]
!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_PROFILE=kb/profiles/agi.p0
!set PARROT0_LANG=en
!reset

[test a curated class property reaches the member, with the reason]
!timeout 30
> is a whale warm-blooded?
< Yes: a whale is a mammal, and every mammal is warm-blooded.
> does copper conduct electricity?
< Yes: copper is a metal, and every metal conducts electricity.

[test a property taught by speaking reaches a member no lesson named]
!timeout 30
> is an eagle warm-blooded?
< Yes: an eagle is a bird, and every bird is warm-blooded.
> is a toad cold-blooded?
< Yes: a toad is an amphibian, and every amphibian is cold-blooded.

[test no is said only with the opposite property, never from absence]
!timeout 30
> is a whale cold-blooded?
< No: a whale is a mammal, and every mammal is warm-blooded.
> do whales lay eggs?
<! No:
<! Yes:

[test mix 02x08x09 an elliptic follow-up inherits the property just asked]
!timeout 30
> is a whale warm-blooded?
<~ Yes: a whale is a mammal
> and a snake?
< No: a snake is a reptile, and every reptile is cold-blooded.
> what about an eagle?
< Yes: an eagle is a bird, and every bird is warm-blooded.
